{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Adw4QNVCx3bVMMAJE7d2hB","type":"tool_result","content":"  that `Counter.render` and `Badge.render` are `undefined` in the\n  browser bundle and that `Notice.render` is still a function.\n- `reveal.ts` -- removes the class that hides the page until it has\n  hydrated.\n- `index.css` -- page-level styles.\n\n`components/` runs on both sides:\n\n- `counter.ts` -- a counter with increment and decrement buttons. Its\n  `.render` returns `html`, nests a `Badge` that shows the current\n  count, and passes `children` through.\n- `badge.ts` -- the smallest possible component.\n- `notice.ts` -- keeps its render function on the client with\n  `{ client: true }`.\n- `counter.css`, `badge.css` -- component styles. Under plain esbuild\n  they load as empty modules (`--loader:.css=empty`).\n\n`server/` runs only in Node:\n\n- `app.ts` -- the Hono app and its routes. It has no Node imports and\n  takes an injectable scaffold loader.\n- `routes.ts` -- the route bodies, written with `html`.\n- `scaffold.ts` -- loads the scaffold and replaces the marker.\n- `listen.ts` -- the production server. It loads the built scaffold,\n  mounts the app, and serves built assets.\n- `ssr.ts` -- the stdout render command.\n- `tsconfig.json` -- type-checks this folder with Node types.\n\n---\n\n## `.render`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88e9b129-578a-4f21-9b36-91ad159ff531","uuid":"83e9389c-80ff-49fd-b272-e60c37d395c9","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:59:55.757Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  that `Counter.render` and `Badge.render` are `undefined` in the\n  browser bundle and that `Notice.render` is still a function.\n- `reveal.ts` -- removes the class that hides the page until it has\n  hydrated.\n- `index.css` -- page-level styles.\n\n`components/` runs on both sides:\n\n- `counter.ts` -- a counter with increment and decrement buttons. Its\n  `.render` returns `html`, nests a `Badge` that shows the current\n  count, and passes `children` through.\n- `badge.ts` -- the smallest possible component.\n- `notice.ts` -- keeps its render function on the client with\n  `{ client: true }`.\n- `counter.css`, `badge.css` -- component styles. Under plain esbuild\n  they load as empty modules (`--loader:.css=empty`).\n\n`server/` runs only in Node:\n\n- `app.ts` -- the Hono app and its routes. It has no Node imports and\n  takes an injectable scaffold loader.\n- `routes.ts` -- the route bodies, written with `html`.\n- `scaffold.ts` -- loads the scaffold and replaces the marker.\n- `listen.ts` -- the production server. It loads the built scaffold,\n  mounts the app, and serves built assets.\n- `ssr.ts` -- the stdout render command.\n- `tsconfig.json` -- type-checks this folder with Node types.\n\n---\n\n## `.render`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
