{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi78Q1HKcc76jqETCi22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Every route's response has the root element containing the navigation and the page, and the scaffold file itself contains no navigation\n[x] Exactly one navigation link carries `aria-current` on each known route, and it is the link for that route; none on the 404\n[x] The route table returns the not-found page for an unknown route\n[x] The index page accepts heading and label as arguments and the existing escaping test still passes through them\n[x] The state script from ticket 08 is still present and round-trips\n[x] `server/routes.ts` no longer exists and nothing imports it\n[x] The existing e2e suite passes: nav links reach every route and the runtime assertions contain no FAIL\n[x] `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:hydration-dev`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run typecheck:hydration` pass\n\nTicket 09 is done and committed as `bb6bd48` (one commit, since the checklist items all depend on each other). Every suite named in the ticket passes, as do the full `npm test` (217/217) and the e2e suite (8/8). `npm run lint` fails with two errors in `test/plugins.ts`, which I didn't touch, so I left them alone.\n\n**What changed:**\n1. **New `example-hydration/pages/`:** one page function per route (`index`, `list`, `notice`, `not-found`), plus `layout.ts` and `routes.ts`. The layout renders the nav and `<main>`, and binds each link's `aria-current` to the `route` signal. `routes.ts` has a `pageFor(route)` lookup that returns the not-found page for unknown routes.\n2. **Index page:** heading and label are now plain arguments to the index page, still passed through `createApp({ index })`.\n3. **Scaffold:** the nav is gone from `index.html`. The page marker sits inside `<div id=\"root\">`, followed by the assertions section, the state marker and the module script.\n4. **Server:** `server/app.ts` renders the layout around the page for each route and converts it to a string. `server/routes.ts` is deleted.\n5. **Client:** `client/index.ts` now null-checks the notice button and target, which only the notice route renders.\n\n**Change outside the ticket's file list:** I added `--loader:.css=empty` to the first `test/hydration.ts` command in `package.json`'s `test:hydration` script. The test now imports `pages/` from source, which pulls in component CSS, and without the flag esbuild fails to build. Worse, `test:hydration` didn't fail when that happened: that suite ran zero tests while the listener suite still showed passes. Note this also applies to the current script for anyone importing a module that loads CSS.\n\n**Known gap:** on `/index.html` no nav link is marked current, because the route there is `/index.html`, not `/`. Nothing in the tests checks that path.\n\nI updated `AGENTS.md` and the example README for the new `pages/` directory.\n\nThe Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Drive and Netlify connectors need authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings, and the `aws-mcp` server failed to connect. This ticket didn't need any of them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":69889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":701,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88e9b129-578a-4f21-9b36-91ad159ff531","uuid":"f1aff5e3-7b4f-4f94-8c67-5d9a95bed896","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:00:16.904Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi78PY13AdrpSA94tuMN"}
